A||||9||speed racer||no cat ||||1||
Z||000000||speed racer||01-10-2001||07:20 PM||||Has any one taken off their cat.? If so how does it sound and do you recommend it||||reg||1
Z||000001||MrPBody||01-10-2001||07:36 PM||||I temporarily removed my cat (<I>Shhhhh!</I> Don't tell!) while waiting for a replacement from Rodney.  My '85 2.5 with stock muffler was noticeably louder but not too obnoxious.  My wife didn't notice.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||speed racer||01-10-2001||07:44 PM||||Also does it sound the same but louder||||reg||1
Z||000003||MrPBody||01-10-2001||08:04 PM||||Yep, pretty much.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||rockcrawl||01-10-2001||09:58 PM||||I hollowed mine out and put it back on so it still looks like there's one on there for future emisions inspections. It has a funny ringing or resonating sound at certain RPMs, hard to describe. Not too much louder than stock either. A lot better than hearing chunks of catalyst rattling around inside.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000005||Standard||01-11-2001||03:14 AM||||I think the v6 sounds pretty sweet w/o a cat.. but I think I'm gonna replace my straight pipe with a hi-flow cat after i get done with my engine.. than I'll leave off the muffler and put on a pair of resonator tips to annoy the neighbors  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||
Z||000006||overlord||01-11-2001||08:48 AM||||mines goin in the shop today..in 3.5 hours to be exact to get cat removed.(clogged and leaking exhaust).<BR>With the tiny little muffler thats on now, its gonna be pretty loud for a 2.5||||reg||1
Z||000007||ChadMan||01-11-2001||09:22 AM||||You'll be surprised, Overlord.  A couple of years ago I removed the clogged cat from my 88 Coupe and replaced it with a cherry bomb (kept the original muffler) - it was slightly louder, not much.<P>I recently replaced the cherry bomb with a new cat.  Slightly quieter - not much.<P>Now if you remove the muffler...cat or no cat, it will be loud as all hell and annoying too.||||reg||1
Z||000008||overlord||01-11-2001||04:18 PM||||just got fiero out of teh shop.<BR>Turns out the cat had all ready been gutted but still had a hole in it so they just patched it up. Guess it was as loud as it was gonna get. I also have cherry bomb muffler...||||reg||1
Z||000009||Ronnie||01-11-2001||10:11 PM||||My muffler had developed an annoying rattle in it when hot.Went to the local junk yard to pick up some other parts.There was a whole exhaust system lying there, chrome tips and all, with a pipe welded in , instead of the cat. All  I had to do was replace the system on my car.Now has a good muffler and no cat! Has a deeper rumble than before, and runs better too.Can hear the rumble a little better from the drivers seat.||||reg||1
